            <ArticleTitle>Structure-activity relationships of alpha-amino acid ligands for the alpha2delta subunit of voltage-gated calcium channels.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1138-41</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A series of alpha-amino acids were identified as ligands which compete with gabapentin for binding to the alpha(2)delta subunit of voltage-dependent Ca(2+) channels. Potent analogs were identified. Their activity in an in vivo pain assay is described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
